                "fontFamily": "Inter",
                "text": "The hardware says input 2; you say mic. Each chip is a COLUMN \u2014 the name on top, `input 2` under it in grey \u2014 so the socket is always legible and the name is only what you call it. An unnamed chip is the bare `input 3`, centred, in the primary ink (see settings-inputs-unnamed for why the tone moves). Tapping a chip renames it; see settings-inputs-wide for an 18-in rig (#528)."
              }
            ],
